WEBVTT

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.580
Shut your pieholes!

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.710
What happened?

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.460
Why are we here?

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.460
Today, we're being blessed
with a Star Bearer's wisdom.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.840
This is about that phantom mayhem.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.760
One of your teams' lazy
cleaning habits caused this!

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.390
I'm here to question you until
we get to the bottom of it!

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.570
Watchers in the Night

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.820
All right, next!

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.280
Get back to cleaning if I'm done with you!

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.120
Next, we have dimwitted Rose.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.870
It was <i>your </i>team that
let those scorches slip by.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.580
Explain yourself!

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.500
That wasn't a matter
of anything slipping by.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.880
We were holding class that day, and--

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.170
You're always rambling!

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.220
You people were neglecting
your cleaning duties!

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:39.100
Our newest member, Emilico,
was still being trained.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.310
And we had never faced such a disturbance,
hence our delayed response.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.640
But we dealt with it accordingly.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.900
We did not neglect our cleaning.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.820
I'd be happy to submit
our work for your inspection.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.190
I understand perfectly now.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.660
This whole team is a bunch of dimwits.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.580
Watch it, bigmouth!
I was talking to your team leader.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.170
You kicked her! How mean!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:13.710
You're the one who was
waving at me from that window.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.970
I see you're one of those sunshiney types.
You think I'm mean?

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:21.390
Are you criticizing how I do my job?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.480
Barbie, look out!

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.350
Are you hurt?

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.770
You maggot!

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.360
How dare you bump into me?!

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.150
Forgive me. My eyesight is poor.
It was not my intention to bump into you.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.360
Wear glasses if you
have trouble seeing people!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.990
My master doesn't wear glasses,
so wouldn't it be odd for me to?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.290
You dare talk back to me?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.800
That's no way to speak to Barbie.
She's a Star Bearer!

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.380
You're the black sheep of our team.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.430
What now?!

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.310
F-For... Forgive me.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.600
F-F-Forgive me.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.560
You.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.360
You're the most inept of all.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:18.780
You're always dropping things and
scattering the soot you've collected.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.780
I've read the reports.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.910
You can't fool me.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.950
That phantom mayhem was <i>your </i>fault!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.830
That's not--

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.880
She's part of our team,
isn't she? Please help her!

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:34.710
What?

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:38.050
Why? The truth is we cannot do a thing.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:41.470
Plus, she has been nothing
but trouble for our team.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.810
B-But all the blame will be pinned on her.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.640
Someone must take the blame.
It might as well be her.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.350
A doll as inept as her won't
make it past the debut anyway.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.270
She is a failure.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.690
Please, Barbie, don't!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.280
You again?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.990
There must be an explanation.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.870
An explanation?

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.660
All right, in that case...

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.000
Sunshine,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.120
Good-for-Nothing,

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.210
Black Sheep!

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:12.920
Huh?

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.250
She means you.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.500
I hereby assign you
three to the night watch.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.050
I'll see that your rooms
are left unlocked.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:25.100
I'll report your ineptness to the adults
in the other wing if you fail.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.760
What is your name?

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.720
I'm Ricky.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.060
Out of all the new dolls,
you're the only promising one.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.560
Thank you.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.980
Everyone, back to your cleaning!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.110
Your work is not done!

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:42.780
We're not done because of Barbie.
She's abusing the new dolls!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.530
And, Emilico, no good will
come of standing up for others.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.870
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.000
You really should avoid provoking Barbie.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.540
Her shadow master is
a very important figure.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.290
Still, it is nothing
you need to fret over.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.590
Barbie will soon lose interest in this.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:21.860
Oh, welcome back, Emilico.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.450
It's good to be back, Mistress Kate.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.740
Might you be available tonight?

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.830
It would be nice to study together.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:35.170
Oh, forgive me. Tonight,
I have work outside your room.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:38.290
But I would love to some other time!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.510
Is that so? Be careful out there.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:47.140
Yes, ma'am! But before that,
I'll clean your room until it sparkles!

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.570
Really? A Star Bearer already praised you?
That's quite impressive, Ricky.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.030
There's this one doll who's
the black sheep of our team.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:14.710
But I showed him his place,
and none too gently.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.370
Excellent work.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:21.380
I simply did what was befitting
of your face, Master Patrick.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:41.900
Good evening, I'm Emilico.
Let's do the best job we can!

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:44.860
So, what are your names?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.410
I'm Shaun.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:53.040
Well, um, shall we start our watch?

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.290
We'll find something if we look around!

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:59.630
"Something," you say? As if new
dolls like us could solve anything.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:03.500
We have plenty of time before
the major house cleaning in one week.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.090
We'll do just fine.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.220
Nothing unusual in this room.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.480
Huh? Where's Shaun?

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.480
Oh, there he is.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.400
We're over here!

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.780
Oh, right. You can't see very well.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.910
That wasn't me you saw.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.620
What?!

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:38.290
Oh, no. Now that other
doll is falling behind.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.890
Nothing unusual here, either.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:06.070
Wait. Did we already look in here?

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:11.570
How is this watch duty
going to help my master?

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:22.670
Let's do our best again tomorrow.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.730
This is our fifth night.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:26.270
I really hope we can get to the
bottom of that phantom mayhem.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.440
Shaun!

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.280
Did you bring something that might help?

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.200
Blankets.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.950
Blankets? What for?

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:36.820
To sleep.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.080
But why?

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:41.160
They lock our doors
once we leave our rooms.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.210
So I'll sleep here till our time is up.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:45.920
But we only have until
the day after tomorrow.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:50.210
Barbie just wants to sow discord
between our masters and us.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.680
My daily cleaning is starting
to suffer from my lack of sleep.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.760
And you, Emilico?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:00.810
I did Mistress Kate a disservice
by oversleeping this morning.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:05.520
B-But blaming it on someone
else without reason isn't right!

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:11.070
We are our masters' faces. How can we
fulfill our role if we look all worn out?

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:14.360
I only take my master's
instructions seriously.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.240
Please don't give up yet!

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.490
I brought something that will help.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:23.790
It's a map! Mia from
our team drew it for me.

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:28.830
Let's look around together.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:29.840
Wait.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:32.380
So then you <i>will </i>help us?

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.050
I brought blankets for both of you.

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.930
Sleep if you want.
That's all I have to say.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.720
Oh, thank you.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.720
Shall we sleep, then?

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:46.850
It's true, we shouldn't overdo it.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:52.320
I'm not used to this.
It's hard to fall asleep.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.320
The ceiling is so high.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:58.860
And I've never had anyone
next to me as I fall asleep.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:03.620
You're right, Shaun.
It's also important to sleep.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:07.710
And you may try to hide it,
but I can tell you care about us.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.590
After all, you helped me
during Barbie's scolding.

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:14.710
I only did it because she irritated me.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:21.680
I-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:24.720
L-Let's forget about watch duty.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:28.810
I'm nothing but trouble for you two.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.820
I-It's because I'm a failure.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:35.780
Nobody even needs me.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:36.940
I'm sorry.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.280
Hurray!

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:41.780
I'm so glad you finally spoke!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.530
You're no trouble.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:48.830
I'm so happy I became
friends with you and Shaun.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.920
I've also been called a failure.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:56.420
But Mistress Kate protects me anyway.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:13:01.470
Somebody needs you.
There isn't anyone who isn't needed.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:05.260
I want to be friends with you.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.890
I want to be friends
with you, too, of course!

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.190
Um, what I mean is...

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:12.730
Rum.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:16.020
My name is Rum.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.360
Rum!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.030
What a wonderful name!

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.540
Hey.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:28.750
Something's coming.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.460
Could it be a phantom?

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.350
Rum!

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.690
Shaun, it's a phantom! Let's run!

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.190
No, wait.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.900
It's a veiled doll.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.280
What's a veiled doll?

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.410
You've never seen one before?

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.580
They bring us our food and clean clothes.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.750
Oh, so that's who does that!

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.540
Thank you for all your help!

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:15.750
We're trying to get to the
bottom of the phantom mayhem.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:20.550
Don't waste your breath.
Unlike us, veiled dolls don't speak.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.680
It most likely heard our voices
and came to see what's going on.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.640
Oh! We better go after Rum!

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.440
Where am I?

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:38.730
Please talk to me, Rummy.
I'm scared of the dark.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.030
Rum, do you think they will come save you?

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:43.740
Who do you mean?

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.610
That doll.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:49.700
She's not coming. The phantom got her.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.330
Even if it didn't, she won't come.

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:55.710
I left them behind and ran.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:59.290
Still, I have a feeling
she will come for you.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:03.920
Living dolls are expendable.
Only the outstanding ones last very long.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.720
It wouldn't make sense for her
to care about another doll.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.600
Wouldn't you be happy if she did come?

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:16.810
Happy? I don't know
what it feels like to be happy.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:20.150
Rum? Where are you? Rum?

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.690
Rum?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.990
You're a strange one.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:26.950
Strange? Mistress Kate said that, too!

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.200
"Fret not over trivial matters."

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:33.250
That's one of the rules living dolls
learn from the time they are born.

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:38.710
We live for the sake of our masters.
It's pointless to worry about other dolls.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:41.550
It seems I'm not an outstanding doll.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.090
You're right, Shaun.

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:46.050
I should only concern
myself with Mistress Kate.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:50.300
But the way you defied Barbie
wasn't a good idea, either, was it?

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.140
It's true.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.890
That was of no benefit to my master.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:58.770
I'm not an outstanding doll, either.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.030
Would you like a roll?

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.950
Why do you have a roll in your pocket?

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.240
Shaun, you smiled!

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.580
What do you mean?

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:14.870
I thought your face might be ceramic.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:18.210
Our expressions are for our masters.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:22.800
But your cheeks will harden
if you don't move your face.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.630
You have a point.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:29.220
There's still no sign of Rum.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:32.140
What about that map of yours?

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:35.020
Oh, I forgot about that!

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:38.270
We've already searched the great hall.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.190
We still haven't tried

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:44.110
the hallway that leads to the front door.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.080
Mia left a note saying
we mustn't go there.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.540
I'm not surprised.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.460
Venturing outside the house,

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:04.630
let alone entering this hallway,
is strictly forbidden.

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:09.680
Nevertheless, I'm going.
We must find Rum before dawn!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.400
Wait!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:39.910
Does this mean that all who try to leave
Shadows House are immediately eliminated?

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.960
Would they really go so far?

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.630
Living dolls have thoughts and feelings

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:49.590
and wish to be of service
to their shadow masters.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:52.050
"Fret not over trivial matters."

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:55.550
That's a rule living dolls must follow.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:18:00.430
Let's head back. There's no way
Rum made it through this hallway.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.860
Rum!

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:08.360
It came from behind this wall!
Show me the map!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.070
I don't see a door that leads there.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.820
A door?

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.910
I know how to get there!

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:22.460
Huh?

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:25.250
It's just like our rooms!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.590
So that's it! A revolving door!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:36.140
Emilico! Did you find anything?

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:38.010
It's too dark to see!

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.020
My whole body aches from
plunging through the door!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:44.520
If you knew about the door,
you could've opened it normally.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.360
You're absolutely right.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.610
Ouch! I just ran into a wall.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:51.150
Wait for me. I'll be right there.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.280
Rum!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:01.790
We were worried about you!
Are you all right?

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:06.210
We heard you scream. Did something happen?

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:10.380
S-S... Scorches!

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:13.920
Don't worry. I've dealt with them before!

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.970
Take that, and that!

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.970
Rum! Light up the room!

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:18.890
Take that!

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.470
And that!

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:29.360
A phantom!

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.940
So this is where they're coming from.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:33.820
But I didn't bring any water!

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:37.360
That was a big mistake.
Water works great on phantoms!

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:41.660
We'll have to clobber it!
Try to hold it still.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.330
Leave it to me!

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:44.200
But, um...

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.870
How exactly do I do that?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:47.710
Here it comes!

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:50.340
Um... uh... Oh!

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:52.710
Shaun, let me borrow this.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.680
Keep screaming so I know where you are!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:07.100
The phantom is above my head!
That's your right, no left!

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:13.400
If I get close enough,
I can figure it out myself!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:14.940
You smashed it to bits.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.070
You're really strong, Shaun!

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.410
Tie it up just in case.

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:25.080
Our work's not done!

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.290
Look at that!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.290
At what?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:33.170
The trapdoor on the ceiling is loose,
and soot is leaking out.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:36.050
What's soot doing up there?

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.390
Hey!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:58.820
So that's it! Soot from each
room passes through the attic!

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.370
That's where the soot is leaking from.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:05.950
The hinge rusted and broke,
causing the trapdoor to crack open.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:10.040
The soot leaking from there
collected until it became a phantom.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.540
So that's it.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:16.000
It was nobody's fault! Case solved!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.390
Now let's celebrate! Here's a roll!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.850
I don't need any.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:34.400
Yum!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.110
Isn't this the bread
the Shadows family eats?

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:39.110
Mistress Kate shares it with me.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.490
I wanted everyone to try it.

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:44.740
She's that close to her master?

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.410
She really is a strange one.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.790
Is it yummy, Rum?

00:21:55.920 --> 00:22:00.420
How much longer will Emilico
be working outside this room?

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:06.430
We promised to share information.

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:10.430
At this rate, we'll never
make it past the debut.

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:16.610
There is something that Kate needs to do.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:51.990
NEXT EPISODE

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:51.990
"THE DEBUT"

00:23:48.950 --> 00:23:51.490
Next episode, "The Debut."
